# UI — shadcn/ui

- Before adding UI, use the shadcn MCP to check availability and pull the latest (if MCP is configured; otherwise use `npx shadcn` + ui.shadcn.com).
- Use the preset from `components.json` (do not invent a new preset).
- Prefer `@/components/ui/*` before custom UI.
- Follow ui.shadcn.com structure, composition, and naming.
- Do not invent custom button, input, dialog, select, table, or form primitives if shadcn already provides them.
- Reuse shadcn variants / CVA instead of ad-hoc styles.
- Forms: shadcn form patterns + accessible labels and errors.
- Full responsive is required (PRD D40).
